WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.467 --> 00:00:01.167 line:92%
-I am a big fan of yours.

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:03.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was wondering, you're doing
this "Good Wife" spinoff.

00:00:03.837 --> 00:00:04.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I am.
-Were you a fan of

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:07.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
"The Good Wife"
before you took this on?

00:00:07.374 --> 00:00:08.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Very much so.
Very much so.

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:11.411 align:start size:94% position:6%
I loved "The Good Wife,"
and -- and I was --

00:00:11.411 --> 00:00:13.213 size:81% position:41%
I was ecstatic to hear
that there was going

00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:15.782 align:start size:94% position:6%
to be an extension
to the series.

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:17.717
So I kind of like jumped
at the chance of being able

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:19.252 align:start size:94% position:6%
to be a part
of "The Good Fight."

00:00:19.252 --> 00:00:20.153 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Yes. It's very nice.

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:21.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-You're a good fit.

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:23.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
You play a lawyer this year
whose father

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:26.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
is sort of a Bernie Madoff
type character.

00:00:26.126 --> 00:00:29.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
A ponzi schemer,
to say the least.

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:31.498
And I was wondering were you
familiar with Bernie Madoff?

00:00:31.498 --> 00:00:34.134
Certainly those of us here
in New York were very familiar.

00:00:34.134 --> 00:00:35.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I'm sure you guys were.
Yeah.

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:36.503 line:92%
-Yeah. It was a big deal.

00:00:36.503 --> 00:00:39.639
Some of us -- some of us did not
come out that well.

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:40.874 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Yeah.

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:44.044 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I suddenly remember reading
about Bernie Madoff

00:00:44.044 --> 00:00:47.180
and reading about ponzi schemes
and realizing

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:49.616 size:75% position:38%
just how they ruined
and devastate lives.

00:00:49.616 --> 00:00:52.752 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I remember being intrigued
kind of like while I was

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:55.655
reading the article thinking
how extraordinary it would be

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:59.526
to be in the kind of inner
circle of the Madoff family

00:00:59.526 --> 00:01:02.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
and how -- and what the like
repercussions would be

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:05.098 line:92%
to be -- to being involved.

00:01:05.098 --> 00:01:05.698 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And as a result,

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:07.200
kind of like reading the script
for "The Good Fight."

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.636 size:88% position:44%
That -- I kind of leapt
at the chance of playing

00:01:09.636 --> 00:01:11.304 align:start size:94% position:6%
Maia, who very much
felt betrayed

00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:13.973 align:start size:94% position:6%
by her father
just being a crook.

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:15.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And a really, really kind

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:16.810 line:92%
of like, yeah, horrible man.

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:19.679 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You -- your family
not a single real life

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:20.847 align:start size:94% position:6%
ponzi schemer in the bunch,
right?

00:01:20.847 --> 00:01:21.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, thank God. No.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.848 --> 00:01:24.284
-And also not a single --
-No, we're wholesome like that.

00:01:24.284 --> 00:01:25.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wholesome.
-Very wholesome.

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:27.854 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You were the only actor
in the lot.

00:01:27.854 --> 00:01:28.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I am.
-Was your family --

00:01:28.755 --> 00:01:30.623 align:start size:94% position:6%
a big family, right?
Four siblings?

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:31.458 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Five.
-Five siblings.

00:01:31.458 --> 00:01:32.292 line:92%
-Oh, sorry, sorry, you're right.

00:01:32.292 --> 00:01:33.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
Five kids, so four siblings.
-Gotcha.

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:35.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
No worries. I tricked you.
I tricked you.

00:01:35.228 --> 00:01:38.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You did. You did.
Who uses the word siblings?

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:40.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Exactly.
It was my fault.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:41.935 align:start size:94% position:6%
But did they --
were they excited

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:43.169 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you went into acting?
-They were.

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:45.038 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did they --
when did they start to care?

00:01:45.038 --> 00:01:46.039 line:92%
-When did they start to care?

00:01:46.039 --> 00:01:47.340 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I think my sisters
very much

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
were kind of like backing me
from the get-go.

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:50.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-My parents, obviously,

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:52.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
always been incredibly
supportive.

00:01:52.512 --> 00:01:54.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then my brothers
only really began

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:56.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
to give a [bleep]
when I got "Game of Thrones."

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:58.151 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:58.151 --> 00:01:58.952 align:start size:94% position:6%
Only then
-That's a real...

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:02.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Only then. I was terrible.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:04.257 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And then --

00:02:04.257 --> 00:02:06.526 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they're kind of like
beginning to call up

00:02:06.526 --> 00:02:07.494 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they'll be like,
"Oh, okay.

00:02:07.494 --> 00:02:09.896 align:start size:94% position:6%
So what are the new scripts
coming through?

00:02:09.896 --> 00:02:10.897 line:92%
And what are you, like, up for?"

00:02:10.897 --> 00:02:13.199 align:start size:94% position:6%
and prior to that,
they didn't --

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:13.800 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
they did not care.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:16.669
-I think -- I was probably --
I think I probably saw you

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:17.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
first in "Downton Abbey."
-Right.

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:19.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then next
in "Game of Thrones."

00:02:19.439 --> 00:02:21.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
And a massive
difference between

00:02:21.441 --> 00:02:22.609 align:start size:94% position:6%
the two characters
you played as well.

00:02:22.609 --> 00:02:24.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Absolutely.
-As far as the amount of range

00:02:24.444 --> 00:02:26.813 size:75% position:38%
I saw from the first
two times I saw you,

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:28.314 line:92%
just massively well done.

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:29.182 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh. [ Laughs ]

00:02:29.182 --> 00:02:31.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Just the first one wanted
to be a secretary.

00:02:31.184 --> 00:02:33.186 size:84% position:42%
The next one, very good
with a bow and arrow.

00:02:33.186 --> 00:02:34.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Very good, yeah.
She was blood thirsty.

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:36.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Blood thirsty.
-She was blood thirst,

00:02:36.456 --> 00:02:37.757 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it was great,
because I didn't have to wear

00:02:37.757 --> 00:02:38.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
a corset in "Game of Thrones."
-Yeah.

00:02:38.858 --> 00:02:41.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I Mean I was relived.
-Yeah, just like a heavy fur.

00:02:41.528 --> 00:02:42.428 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Just a heavy fur. Yeah.

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:46.032
Just tons of rabbits, like,
falling off your shoulder.

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:47.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So you --
for those who don't know,

00:02:47.534 --> 00:02:48.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
you met Kit Harington
on that show.

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:50.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
You guys are engaged.
-We are, we are.

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:52.872
-Congratulations.
-Thank you very much. Thank you.

00:02:52.872 --> 00:02:54.207 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:54.207 --> 00:02:55.108 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It is. It's lovely.

00:02:55.108 --> 00:02:58.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You are -- now you're in a
situation where he's on

00:02:58.945 --> 00:03:01.814 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Game of Thrones"
and he is getting --

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:04.083 align:start size:94% position:6%
do you try to get
information from him?

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:05.218 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Gasps ] No.
-Okay.

00:03:05.218 --> 00:03:06.753 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, talk about
being an avid fan.

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:07.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
I obviously am
of "The Good Wife,"

00:03:07.787 --> 00:03:09.889
but with "Game of Thrones,"
I'm like rest of the world.

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:12.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like waited --
I'm waiting for the new --

00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:14.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-The new and final season.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:14.961 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-I know, heartbreaking.

00:03:14.961 --> 00:03:15.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Obviously,
kind of heartbreaking.

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:17.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't know
what I'm going to do.

00:03:17.063 --> 00:03:17.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, God,
what are we gonna to do?

00:03:17.997 --> 00:03:20.099
-I don't know. Move on
to another thing I guess.

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:21.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
"The Good Fight?"

00:03:21.301 --> 00:03:22.335 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, exactly.
"The good Fight."

00:03:22.335 --> 00:03:23.903 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, there we go.
Thank you.

00:03:23.903 --> 00:03:27.440
-But no, so I remember kind
of like, over in the summer.

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:29.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
Summer just gone, obviously,
the new episodes

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:31.544 size:75% position:38%
for the final season
were coming through

00:03:31.544 --> 00:03:33.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
onto his iPad and I --
I mean,

00:03:33.213 --> 00:03:34.714 align:start size:94% position:6%
I can read
his facial expressions.

00:03:34.714 --> 00:03:35.982
-Yeah.
-I didn't want to know anything

00:03:35.982 --> 00:03:37.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's going on,
like within his eyes

00:03:37.217 --> 00:03:39.619 size:84% position:42%
or anything like that.
So, I sent him packing.

00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:41.754 size:84% position:42%
I kind of like boot him
out so that he can go

00:03:41.754 --> 00:03:43.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
to the coffee shop.
-Oh, so you won't let him even

00:03:43.323 --> 00:03:44.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
read it in front of you.
-Absolutely not.

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:46.826 size:81% position:41%
No, because I'll know,
I'll be able to gage.

00:03:46.826 --> 00:03:48.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Gotcha.
-Like, if he stiffens

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:50.296 align:start size:94% position:6%
then I know that --
someone's dead.

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:51.297 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-And then I'm like,

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:52.765 align:start size:94% position:6%
"No, I don't,"
and then my mind goes off.

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:54.133 align:start size:94% position:6%
-By the way, I don't want
to ruin it for you,

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:55.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
someone's going to be dead.
-You think?

00:03:55.802 --> 00:03:56.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah
-You think?

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:57.804 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, it would be great
if it was, like,

00:03:57.804 --> 00:03:59.305 align:start size:94% position:6%
the last season of
"Game of Thrones,"

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:00.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
nobody dies.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:03.309
That's one hell of a twist.
-That would be a great twist.

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:04.477 line:92%
-Yeah, that would be a twist.

00:04:04.477 --> 00:04:05.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I want to ask --
speaking of a twist,

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:08.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
this seems like a very cruel
prank that --

00:04:08.848 --> 00:04:10.583 size:78% position:39%
this was April Fools.
-This is April Fools.

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:12.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is last year.
-Last year's April Fools.

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:15.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-So your lovely fiance,

00:04:15.955 --> 00:04:16.656 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Kit, did this to you.

00:04:16.656 --> 00:04:18.057 align:start size:94% position:6%
You opened up --
this is your refrigerator.

00:04:18.057 --> 00:04:20.793
-This is our refrigerator
back at home in London,

00:04:20.793 --> 00:04:23.429 align:start size:94% position:6%
and bearing in mind
I had just wrapped

00:04:23.429 --> 00:04:24.964 align:start size:94% position:6%
from season one
of "The Good Fight."

00:04:24.964 --> 00:04:27.333 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I had been in New York
for about six months.

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:29.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
We hadn't spent not
a lot of time together,

00:04:29.302 --> 00:04:33.906
and then I go home and then the
bastard puts this in the fridge.

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:34.907 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:34.907 --> 00:04:36.009 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Oh, boy.

00:04:36.009 --> 00:04:37.310 line:92%
And look, you went to town.

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:39.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-He went to town. He...

00:04:39.646 --> 00:04:43.049 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's amazing.
-Decorated it with blue wings.

00:04:43.049 --> 00:04:43.449 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh.

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:46.653 size:84% position:42%
I mean, that is just --
did you fully scream?

00:04:46.653 --> 00:04:47.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I fully screamed.
-Yeah.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:49.756
-Oh, I fully screamed,
so basically there's this

00:04:49.756 --> 00:04:51.758 align:start size:94% position:6%
whole big thing
with the Brita filter.

00:04:51.758 --> 00:04:55.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I basically had ordered
a Brita filter the day before,

00:04:55.428 --> 00:04:57.397 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was very excited
about its arrival.

00:04:57.397 --> 00:04:59.332 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'd been on the Internet
kind of like looking at

00:04:59.332 --> 00:05:01.567 align:start size:94% position:6%
the different models
and couldn't wait

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:02.235 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
for filtered water.

00:05:02.235 --> 00:05:05.305
And so kind of like went
downstairs to the fridge,

00:05:05.305 --> 00:05:07.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was getting ready
to kind of like

00:05:07.073 --> 00:05:09.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
have my glass of water
for the first one of the day.

00:05:09.409 --> 00:05:10.877 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was chatting
to him over there,

00:05:10.877 --> 00:05:12.979 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I don't remember him
kind of holding up the phone

00:05:12.979 --> 00:05:15.415 size:78% position:39%
because he took video
of the whole thing.

00:05:15.415 --> 00:05:16.516 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I thought that he was
kind of, like,

00:05:16.516 --> 00:05:18.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
texting but still,
you know, speaking to me.

00:05:18.951 --> 00:05:21.921
And then as I then turn my
attention back to the fridge,

00:05:21.921 --> 00:05:24.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
I see this terrifying head
staring back at me,

00:05:24.991 --> 00:05:27.093 size:88% position:44%
and I don't necessarily
recognize that it's him.

00:05:27.093 --> 00:05:30.229
But I just know that somebody's
just bloodied in my --

00:05:30.229 --> 00:05:33.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
like in my fridge,
hairy and -- Oh, God. Horror.

00:05:33.633 --> 00:05:34.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, I thought
it was bad enough,

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:37.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
but the fact that you also
wanted filtered water.

00:05:37.503 --> 00:05:40.840 size:84% position:42%
-Yeah, no. Big time.
That's why I was there.

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:41.407 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Yeah, exactly.

00:05:41.407 --> 00:05:43.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I hope you have plans
on how to get him back.

00:05:43.142 --> 00:05:45.011
You're running out of time.
-I'm running out of time.

00:05:45.011 --> 00:05:46.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know,
the anniversary is coming up.

00:05:46.646 --> 00:05:47.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-First of April.

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:48.948 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-But that's the thing,

00:05:48.948 --> 00:05:49.615 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
like as a family --

00:05:49.615 --> 00:05:51.918 size:75% position:38%
certainly my family,
we don't really do

00:05:51.918 --> 00:05:52.585 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
pranks in that way.

00:05:52.585 --> 00:05:53.953 size:78% position:39%
Like, first of April,
it comes and goes.

00:05:53.953 --> 00:05:56.422
I don't really know many people
who do like big, scary,

00:05:56.422 --> 00:05:58.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
terrifying pranks
-And that's a -- that's a --

00:05:58.191 --> 00:06:00.126
by the way, this is a huge waste
of time and money.

00:06:00.126 --> 00:06:01.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
You don't have to worry
about that.

00:06:01.461 --> 00:06:02.562 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I know. exactly.
Yeah.

00:06:02.562 --> 00:06:05.431 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you so much for being
here. Such a pleasure.

